    {
      "id": "GPL-02",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-good-place-gram-lift",
      "title": "Integral isometries matching a regular Gram frame at almost every finite place",
      "statement": "For rational X with nonsingular Gram matrix and adelic Y of the same Gram matrix, there is a finite set S such that at every finite v outside S an isometry preserving the coordinate lattice sends X to Yᵥ. One S works for every Y in a fixed compact family.",
      "hypotheses": "CM quadratic number fields, nonsingular rational Hermitian form J, finite ambient and frame dimensions. Choose a rational simultaneous diagonalization of the shared Gram matrix. Outside S the rational frames and changes of coordinates, form matrix and inverse, local target frame and phase parameters are integral; all diagonal entries, 2, d and Q are units. Leave all ramified and dyadic places in S.",
      "correspondence": "The source applies the diagonal-column isometry to the adelic coefficient algebra, using a restricted-product choice with integral inverses outside finitely many places. The exposition works coordinatewise over a fixed good local ring. It gives the matrices and integral inverses, tracks their successive action, and obtains a uniform exceptional set on a compact family by a finite subcover. AGF-02 uses this local component to produce an adelic inverse.",
      "dependencies": [
        "AGF-01",
        "GPL-01"
      ],
